# Admin > Compliance > Erasure and scrubbing. These are controls over stored history and backups; whether a deployment meets a given law is for the operator to decide.

admin-nav-erasure-coverage = Erasure and scrubbing
compliance-card-erasure-coverage = Replace one person's identifiers in audit history and logs, and see which backups still hold people who were erased.
admin-erasure-title = Erasure and scrubbing
admin-erasure-intro = Scrub person replaces a person's address and account ids in audit history and in the rotated log files with a stable keyed pseudonym. The audit hash chain is re-sealed so verification still passes. Every erasure and scrub also leaves a tombstone, so a restore of an older backup erases those people again.
admin-erasure-docs = The registry of what is erased, exported and kept for each table is in docs/admin/erasure-coverage.md.
admin-erasure-scrub = Scrub person
admin-erasure-scrub-note = Run the preview first: it counts the rows and log lines that would change and changes nothing.
admin-erasure-address = Address
admin-erasure-preview = Preview
admin-erasure-run = Scrub person
admin-erasure-dry-note = Preview only. Nothing has been changed.
admin-erasure-done-note = Scrubbed. The person now appears as { $pseudonym }.
admin-erasure-nothing = No history names this person.
admin-erasure-col-table = Table or file
admin-erasure-col-rows = Rows
admin-erasure-confirm-title = Scrub this person from history?
admin-erasure-confirm-body = Audit entries and log lines that name the person are rewritten with the pseudonym. This cannot be undone; the address cannot be recovered from the pseudonym without the key.
admin-erasure-settings = Settings
admin-erasure-keys = Pseudonym keys
admin-erasure-keys-note = Pseudonyms are made with the current key generation. Rotating adds a generation; older ones stay until the retention set above removes them.
admin-erasure-rotate = Rotate key
admin-erasure-keys-none = No key has been created yet. The first scrub creates one.
admin-erasure-col-gen = Generation
admin-erasure-col-created = Created
admin-erasure-col-state = State
admin-erasure-key-current = Current
admin-erasure-key-retired = Retired, kept
admin-erasure-key-destroy = Retired, deleted on { $when }
admin-erasure-chain = Audit chain
admin-erasure-chain-note = Each audit entry holds a hash of the one before it. A scrub rewrites entries and re-seals the chain, and records the old and new head hash.
admin-erasure-seal = Seal new entries
admin-erasure-chain-ok = The chain verifies: { $rows } entries sealed, { $unsealed } waiting to be sealed.
admin-erasure-chain-bad = The chain does not verify; first bad entry at position { $seq }.
